{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>It is a נתק.</b> That within the area of hair there is some spot from which the hair has been severed by the force of the illness — not by human agency and not by a chemical preparation — even though there is no visible discoloration there at all, as our Sages of blessed memory received. And so it is a species of צרעת among physicians. He said: if so, then even if discolorations and eruptions that determine impurity appear in the area of the נתק outside a place of hair, behold the black hair preserves a place of hair from the discoloration and from the eruption."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:12.194151279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}